& [DelineationTrace] is the PreparedRuntime subject boundary
  + [inside] is immutable environment-generation identity, cached digest and package binding, exact-scope admitted fabric projection, protocol-equivalent execution, bounded cache replacement, concurrency, activation, invalidation, rollback, memory measurement, latency measurement, proof, and adapter delegation
  + [outside] is changing SOP meaning, changing package signatures, changing query ranking, inventing caller authority, live database mutation, neural routing, FPGA execution, distributed consensus, multi-tenant policy, hidden-state access, and Phase7 activation
  + [references] is canonical JSON persistence, current MCP projection, signed package admission, deterministic query, and future publisher work
  + [uncertainty] is production-corpus heap and workload behavior beyond the measured fixture family
  - never: let performance state become semantic or trust authority
  - never: call a scope projection reusable for a different AuthorityScope

& [ConstraintLedger] is the source-grounded invariant set
  + [source_preservation] is the dictated source remains unchanged and separate
  + [semantic_oracle] is execute_protocol_request and its exact ProtocolResponse remain the correctness oracle
  + [trust_bootstrap] is embedded TrustStore data is subordinate to a supervisor-controlled environment path and independently supplied request digest and package bindings
  + [scope_integrity] is admission remains a function of exact requested_scope
  + [request_gate_integrity] is protocol, caller, purpose, effect, digest, package-set, scope, operation, query, budget, proof, status, exit, fault, and continuation gates remain active
  + [generation_integrity] is environment bytes, trust store, pinned trust time, package order, protocol version, or preparation profile change creates a different generation
  + [invalidation_integrity] is failed replacement or explicit invalidation cannot leave stale authority silently active
  + [ownership_integrity] is retained and peak memory are measured rather than inferred from serialized bytes
  + [bounded_state] is one active scope projection per environment generation unless a later signed specification authorizes a different cache policy
  + [adapter_boundary] is MCP transports requests and responses but owns no semantic decision
  + [evidence_gate] is production activation follows measured equivalence, latency, memory, concurrency, and lifecycle evidence

& [ConstraintCheckTrace] is the grounding and repair record
  + [source_preservation] is grounded in the user objective and Specification Governance
  + [semantic_oracle] is grounded in the user objective, Phase6 proof, and current protocol implementation
  + [trust_bootstrap] is grounded in Phase6 bootstrap analysis
  + [scope_integrity] is grounded in admit_package requiring requested_scope and certificate authority containment
  + [generation_integrity] is grounded in EmbeddedRuntimeEnvironment digesting environment_version, now_epoch_seconds, TrustStore, ordered packages, and package bytes
  + [ownership_integrity] is grounded in the observed package and index cloning path
  + [repair] is replace the vague idea of one globally prepared fabric with an exact-scope projection
  + [repair] is distinguish pinned trust time from an unimplemented trusted wall-clock service
  + [conflict] is none remaining inside the bounded prototype

& [ConceptualDataModel] is the meaning layer
  + [EnvironmentGeneration] is one immutable semantic environment identified by its exact environment digest and preparation profile
  + [RuntimeAuthorityBinding] is the request-supplied environment digest and complete package set that independently bind semantic use
  + [ScopeProjection] is one immutable admitted SemanticFabric valid for exactly one AuthorityScope within one EnvironmentGeneration
  + [PreparedRuntime] is the core director that validates requests and retains at most one ScopeProjection for an EnvironmentGeneration
  + [PreparedRuntimeSlot] is the activation boundary that exposes zero or one whole PreparedRuntime generation
  + [GenerationTransition] is an atomic activation, replacement, invalidation, or rollback event
  + [RuntimeMetrics] is non-authoritative observation of preparation, hit, miss, latency, retained heap, peak heap, and concurrency behavior

& [LogicalDataModel] is the constraint-bearing structure
  + [generation_natural_key] is environment_digest plus prepared_runtime_profile plus protocol_version
  + [scope_projection_natural_key] is generation_natural_key plus canonical exact AuthorityScope
  + [environment_source] is the immutable EmbeddedRuntimeEnvironment retained for exact fallback and new-scope preparation
  + [derived_projection] is SemanticFabric plus admitted package identities for one exact requested_scope
  + [source_to_projection] is deterministic admission and fabric construction
  + [freshness_rule] is projection current only while generation identity and exact requested_scope are unchanged
  + [recompute_rule] is re-admit from environment_source and atomically replace the complete projection
  + [invalidation_rule] is generation replacement or explicit invalidation removes the old generation from new request selection
  + [rollback_rule] is prepare and activate a separately supplied independently bound prior environment as a new transition
  - never: patch an admitted fabric or generation identity in place

& [PhysicalModelCandidate] is bounded safe Rust
  + [environment_ownership] is shared immutable ownership inside one runtime generation
  + [scope_projection_ownership] is shared immutable ownership selected through a lock-protected single-entry slot
  + [request_read_path] is clone current generation or projection handle, release coordination lock, then execute read-only
  + [scope_change_path] is prepare an entire projection under exact scope and replace the projection slot as one value
  + [generation_change_path] is prepare an entire runtime then compare-and-replace the active slot as one value
  + [in_flight_rule] is a request that acquired a generation before replacement may finish against that exact snapshot while every later acquisition observes the new state
  + [inactive_rule] is a slot with no active generation refuses execution outside ProtocolResponse rather than fabricating semantic proof
  + [dependency_rule] is use Rust standard synchronization and existing production dependencies unless measurement proves otherwise

& [TrustBootstrapDepthContract] is authority before preparation
  + [activation_trigger] is a supervisor supplies an environment and later sends a complete ProtocolRequest
  + [actor] is the supervisor controlling environment selection and request bindings
  + [data] is environment digest, ordered signed package set, TrustStore, pinned trust time, requested scope, and caller context
  + [policy_gate] is request digest and complete package set exactly match the active generation before admission or cache use
  + [proof_gate] is exact response verification and generation metadata
  + [failure_mode] is an attacker controlling environment, request binding, and supervisor trust together remains outside repair by caching
  + [lifecycle] is unbound_environment to request_bound_generation to scope_prepared_generation or trust_fault

& [ScopeProjectionDepthContract] is scope-safe retained execution
  + [activation_trigger] is a request passes environment, protocol, caller, effect, and package binding gates
  + [data] is exact AuthorityScope, admitted packages, SemanticFabric, and admitted package identities
  + [transform] is package admission followed by deterministic fabric construction
  + [policy_gate] is cached requested_scope equals request requested_scope by structural equality
  + [replacement] is a different scope prepares a new complete projection and replaces the prior single projection
  + [proof_gate] is response equals request-scoped execute_protocol_request byte-for-byte after canonical serialization and value-for-value before serialization
  + [failure_mode] is scope mismatch, trust failure, fabric ambiguity, duplicate identity, or resource exhaustion
  - never: reuse a broader, narrower, overlapping, or merely similar scope projection

& [ProtocolEquivalenceDepthContract] is shared gate and outcome construction
  + [activation_trigger] is PreparedRuntime receives ProtocolRequest
  + [interface] is ProtocolRequest to ProtocolResponse with no adapter-specific semantic result
  + [gate_order] is environment version, environment digest, protocol version, caller policy, nonempty packages, exact expected package set, scope admission, fabric construction, operation binding, query scope, query or inspect execution, proof construction, and result verification
  + [query_outcomes] is success, partial unresolved, ambiguity, budget exhaustion, invalid request, policy denial, trust failure, semantic fault, and internal fault where constructible
  + [inspect_outcomes] is fabric, package, certificate, semantic-unit success, unknown identity, proof gap, invalid request, policy denial, and trust failure
  + [equivalence] is exact ProtocolResponse status, exit_class, result, faults, proof, continuation, ordering, and normalized digest
  + [implementation_rule] is direct and prepared paths share request validation and result construction functions
  - never: duplicate protocol policy in the MCP adapter
  - never: replace exact equivalence with selected-field comparison

& [GenerationLifecycleDepthContract] is atomic activation and fail-closed invalidation
  + [state_set] is inactive, active, replacing, invalidated, superseded, or rolled_back
  + [activate] is inactive to active after whole runtime construction
  + [replace] is active generation A to active generation B through expected-generation compare-and-replace
  + [invalidate] is active to inactive through expected-generation compare-and-invalidate
  + [failed_replacement] is active to inactive when a demanded trust, revocation, staleness, or time update cannot prepare safely
  + [stale_transition] is rejected when expected current generation differs from actual current generation
  + [rollback] is inactive or active to a separately reconstructed prior environment after current supervisor binding
  + [proof_gate] is transition receipt identifies previous generation, next generation, and disposition
  + [in_flight_rule] is already acquired immutable snapshots may finish; invalidation controls all later acquisition
  - never: partially mutate an active generation
  - never: silently retain the old generation after a demanded security-state replacement fails

& [TrustTimeDepthContract] is pinned deterministic time
  + [current_model] is now_epoch_seconds belongs to EmbeddedRuntimeEnvironment and therefore its digest
  + [prepared_rule] is use the same pinned trust time as direct execution
  + [time_change] is a new environment generation with a new digest
  + [expiry_boundary] is no live trusted wall-clock enforcement exists in the current protocol
  + [supervisor_duty] is activate a new time-bound environment before relying on changed certificate validity
  + [nonclaim] is PreparedRuntime does not repair the current pinned-time model or claim autonomous wall-clock revocation

& [MemoryOwnershipDepthContract] is measured retained state
  + [baseline] is resident EmbeddedRuntimeEnvironment without a retained admitted fabric
  + [prepared_retained] is environment plus one admitted package/fabric projection plus coordination metadata
  + [prepared_peak] is maximum heap during scope or generation preparation and replacement
  + [measurement] is allocation-level retained and peak bytes in isolated processes over representative sources, units, relations, aliases, quotes, labels, and packages
  + [comparison] is absolute bytes and ratios against the same-process baseline
  + [decision_gate] is measured latency gain must be evaluated with retained and peak memory plus lifecycle complexity
  - never: call serialized JSON size a heap measurement
  - never: retain an unbounded per-scope cache in this slice

& [ConcurrencyDepthContract] is deterministic shared execution
  + [readers] is concurrent requests against one immutable scope projection
  + [writers] is scope replacement, generation replacement, or invalidation
  + [read_rule] is no coordination lock remains held during semantic query or inspection execution
  + [write_rule] is complete replacement becomes visible atomically to later acquisitions
  + [race_rule] is requests use exactly the generation and projection handle they acquired
  + [proof_gate] is repeated mixed query and inspect readers plus replacement races return only complete old or complete new generation outcomes
  + [nonclaim] is no distributed, multiprocess, lock-free, realtime, or fairness guarantee

