& [AcceptanceCriteria] is PR-AC1 through PR-AC14
  + [PR-AC1] is dictated source preserved separately and valid SJS signature issued before implementation
  + [PR-AC2] is PreparedRuntime generation identity binds exact environment digest, profile, protocol, ordered package set, TrustStore, and pinned trust time
  + [PR-AC3] is independent request digest and package bindings pass before a scope projection is used
  + [PR-AC4] is one retained scope projection is valid only for structurally equal AuthorityScope and cross-scope reuse never occurs
  + [PR-AC5] is direct and prepared ProtocolResponse values are exactly equal across query, inspect, success, partial, invalid, trust, policy, unresolved, ambiguity, proof-gap, and budget cases supported by fixtures
  + [PR-AC6] is direct and prepared execution share the same request gates and response construction rather than parallel policy copies
  + [PR-AC7] is immutable concurrent reads are deterministic and no semantic execution holds the projection or generation coordination lock
  + [PR-AC8] is whole-generation activation, replacement, invalidation, stale-transition rejection, failed-security-replacement deactivation, and rollback are tested
  + [PR-AC9] is trust-store revocation, stale package, pinned trust-time change, package change, protocol change, and scope change cannot silently reuse prior prepared state
  + [PR-AC10] is warm preparation, cold process preparation, repeated direct request, repeated prepared request, retained heap, and peak heap are separately measured over representative multi-shape fixtures
  + [PR-AC11] is the adoption record evaluates latency benefit against retained memory, peak memory, lifecycle complexity, limitations, and nonclaims
  + [PR-AC12] is MCP contains no semantic policy and, if activated, delegates to the core PreparedRuntime interface with exact adapter/core equivalence
  + [PR-AC13] is production formatting, lint, debug, release, locked-offline, documentation, and dependency audit gates pass with no unrelated staging
  + [PR-AC14] is solution, proof, feature support, file-change surface, narrative, conversation, and operational-fault records bind the exact implementation and evidence

& [VerificationPlan] is completion evidence
  + [unit] is generation and scope identities, exact binding validation, hit, miss, replacement, invalidation, stale compare, rollback, and unavailable execution
  + [equivalence] is table-driven direct versus prepared ProtocolResponse equality over all constructible outcome families
  + [tamper] is environment, package, trust, time, revocation, staleness, scope, request, proof, and budget mutations
  + [concurrency] is multi-reader same-generation, scope replacement, generation replacement, invalidation, and old-or-new-only result proof
  + [benchmark] is isolated reproducible machine-readable latency and allocation evidence with raw reports, summaries, source hashes, method, and limits
  + [integration] is core, CLI, MCP projection, and live MCP subprocess equivalence where activation occurs
  + [governance] is source hash, artifact existence, unique UUID, signature binding, matrix coverage, and declared-reference resolution

